1          /*==============================================================================
2           * stat_rateci_bug_smethod_all.sas - Bug regression: SMETHOD=ALL omits Blaker
3           *==============================================================================
4           * Macro under test : %stat_rateci
5           * Expected         : SMETHOD=ALL also computes the Blaker interval, as stated
6           *                    in the macro header ("ALL: Requests AC, BLAKER, EXACT,
7           *                    JEFFREYS, WALD and WILSON confidence limits")
8           * Status           : FIXED 2026-10-30 - ALL expanded to AC BLAKER EXACT JEFFREYS LR LOGIT MIDP WALD WILSON
9           * Original defect  : SMETHOD=ALL is forwarded as "cl=(ALL)"; in PROC FREQ the
10          *                    ALL keyword expands to Agresti-Coull, Exact, Jeffreys,
11          *                    Wald and Wilson only, so the Blaker row requested by the
12          *                    macro documentation is silently missing
13          * Fix              : expand ALL explicitly, e.g.
14          *                    cl=(AC BLAKER EXACT JEFFREYS WALD WILSON)
15          * Test passes when  the defect is fixed (run_all then reports FIXED).
16          *============================================================================*/
17         /*--- bootstrap: derive repo root from SYSIN, no absolute paths (qc_env.sas) ---*/
